  "limitations": [
    "Browser proof uses Chromium at 1536x1024 and 390x844 against a fresh local SQLite installation with mock adapters. It does not qualify live providers, production authentication, every catalog workflow, other browsers or physical assistive technology.",
    "The newsletter WRITE workflow intentionally produces a durable mock receipt, not an artifact. Artifact navigation is independently established by the READ-role journey. No external delivery or vendor SDK is enabled.",
    "Connection witness executes the runtime formatter and checks bounded lexical React wiring after removing comments. It is not a TypeScript parser, React renderer or control-flow proof; component tests and real-browser journeys provide separate behavior evidence.",
    "Browser native request and response guards plus instrumented Python child socket guards enforce the tested application-level network boundary. Vite's Node process is not kernel-isolated. Installed dependencies, pinned Node and cached pnpm are prerequisites; the harness performs no acquisition.",
    "Legacy WEB-04 browser regression uses typed read-only configuration and admission-response fixtures. Its genuine full-system counterpart is the dedicated OBJ-06 journey, selected explicitly by the exhaustive aggregate browser inventory.",
    "CI stays disabled; no remote publication, live integrations or final whole-system acceptance is claimed."
  ]
